    "provinceDeepAtlasProfile": {
      "oneLine": "Lun’tharavé is centered at -70.777906, 16.816239 under Participatory Democracy, with 35,306,000 people across 10 settlements.",
      "extremeAtlasDescription": "Lun’tharavé occupies 3,690,965.16 sq mi / 9,559,555.87 sq km of modeled Earth-sized territory, about 1.874181% of Belavadös's surface. It is not merely a province but a continent-scale civic machine: Beach and grass with water, Farming and Partial forest define its broad terrain, while its settlements intensify into Farming, Beach and grass with water and Beach and reefs with water. Population density is 3.693 people/sq km / 9.566 people/sq mi, which lets wilderness, roads, faction-held corridors, and vast uncrowded borders remain huge.",
      "peopleFactionsAndFaith": "The strongest public people-groups are Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, Halfling and Smallfolk, Animalfolk and Mammalian Anthropomorphs, Elf Parent Race and Elf Bloodlines, Amphibious and Aquatic Peoples, Dwarven and Gnomish Kin, and 2 more. Frequently recorded peoples include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin, Harengon, Centaur, Giff, and 4 more. Faction visibility leans toward The Choral Synod, with worship and patronage records naming Nebyrr, Ishtanora, Iskareth, Bastveig, Sokhivar, Sigrananna, Marduthor, and 3 more.",
      "groupLinkDescription": "The province participates in 11 recorded four-province geography group links, including 8 cross-transportation-group links. These links place it inside overlapping regional corridors rather than one isolated block, allowing border-adjacent transit, faction influence, and cultural spillover to breathe across group lines.",
