      "provinceKey": "luntharave",
      "settlement": "Lunévaris",
      "settlementKey": "luntharave:Lunévaris",
      "description": "The Brass Penitent is a masked Verdan mechanist whose public voice promises safety while every private calculation is stained by the people their machines failed to protect. At the Lunevaris Transit Yard, they design containment automata, rescue constructs, and defensive protocols for the Regent Lattice, but their logic keeps circling one terrible conclusion: protection can become murder when compassion is reduced to efficiency. They are brilliant, theatrical, ashamed, and dangerous whenever guilt is allowed to write engineering doctrine.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Lunévaris is a Village in Lun’tharavé, under Participatory Democracy, with low danger, Farming, Beach and grass with water, Mountain range terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Verdan reads through the Verdan entry of the race compendium, within Orcs, Goblins, and Goblinoid Kin, marked by Enkirael. Fey-transformed humanoids who rapidly adapt physically and mentally as they age. They are resilient survivors with an unusually optimistic perspective on change. Table cues: +1 Constitution, +2 Charisma, Black Blood Healing, Limited Telepathy; starting tendency Neutral - Neutral - Neutral - Neutral.",
      "rumors": [
        "The Brass Penitent knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Valkhaday.",
        "The Brass Penitent has a contact in Qasvire who will deny everything."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "The Brass Penitent asks the party to protect a household member without revealing why.",
        "A rival faction offers proof that The Brass Penitent's public story is incomplete."
      ],
